+++ b/docs/TOOLCHAIN.md
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# Toolchain notes
+
+One Homebrew manifest works on both hosts. The Brewfile lists the user space tools. This file records a note for each tool that Homebrew does not provide on Linux, and the source for each such tool.
+
+## Tools from Homebrew
+
+The Brewfile installs virtiofsd, passt, Caddy, socat, GnuPG, swtpm, FreeRDP, wl-clipboard, zenity, libsecret, Ansible, and uv. The phial CLI builds with the Go toolchain from Homebrew.
+
+## Tools that Homebrew does not provide on Linux
+
+- waypipe is not in Homebrew on Linux. Take it from DNF. The root bundle installs it.
+- virt-firmware is not in Homebrew on Linux. It provides virt-fw-vars. Take it from DNF, or run uv tool install virt-firmware.
+- KeePassXC is a Homebrew cask, and casks do not install on Linux. Take it from DNF. Fedora ships KeePassXC.
+- pinentry-gnome3 is not in Homebrew on Linux. Take it from DNF. Fedora ships it.
+- mokutil is not in Homebrew on Linux. Take it from DNF. Fedora ships it.
+- systemd is the host system manager. Homebrew does not provide it. The grants use the user manager over D-Bus.
+- gnome-remote-desktop is a GNOME component. Homebrew does not provide it on Linux. The guest takes it from Fedora packages. GNOME OS ships it.
+
+## Tools with a note
+
+- QEMU is in Homebrew, but the roadmap takes QEMU and waypipe from DNF on the development host. The Fedora build of QEMU carries virglrenderer. Make sure that the QEMU build lists egl-headless and venus with phial-acceptance.
+- notify-send is in libnotify, and Homebrew provides libnotify on Linux. The CLI sends notifications over D-Bus instead, so libnotify is optional.
+
+## Runtime stack notes
+
+- Fedora 45 ships Python 3.15.0rc2. Ansible 2.20 and 2.21 both break against it, because Python 3.15 removed a dataclasses internal. The playbooks pin the guest interpreter to /usr/bin/python3.14 from the python3.14 compat package. The libdnf5 bindings do not exist for that interpreter, so package tasks call the dnf5 command line tool. That tool is C++ and needs no Python.
+- Fedora 45 ships oo7-daemon as the Secret Service. Under passwordless autologin its login collection stays locked, and the unlock prompt has no headless answer. phial therefore uses the gnome-remote-desktop system daemon for RDP. That daemon stores its credentials in the TPM or in a file and needs no Secret Service. The RDP path gives a full remote login session over RDP.
+- The virtio GPU 3D path is broken on the Fedora 45 prerelease stack with QEMU 11.1 rc3, virglrenderer 1.3.0, and Mesa 26.2. The guest kernel times out on GPU capsets with "timed out waiting for cap set 0", and the console framebuffer can freeze. This happens for virgl, venus, and the rutabaga device, on every display backend, and with Fedora 44 and 45 guest kernels alike. The 2D path works. Set PHIAL_GPU to virgl or none until the host stack is fixed. The default PHIAL_GPU=venus turns on blob, venus, and the native context as soon as the stack works.
+- socat resolves the bind= option with the IPv4 resolver inside TCP-LISTEN. For an IPv6 loopback listener use TCP6-LISTEN. The units and the guest dispatcher pick the family themselves.
+- run0 from a login session runs unconfined, so it can execute scripts under the home directory. A run0 call that becomes a transient service runs as init_t, and SELinux then blocks execution of user_home_t files. Pipe the script in that case with run0 bash -s < script.
+- -overcommit mem-lock=on needs LimitMEMLOCK=infinity. The unit sets that limit, and the root bundle lifts the user manager hard limit with a user@.service drop-in.
+- Fedora 45 sshd listens on vsock port 22 natively, and the guest console advertises ssh vsock%3 from the host. Vsock ports below 1024 are privileged, so the socat SSH unit uses port 2222. The host entry and the CLI both dial that port.
+
+## KeePassXC entry convention
+
+The CLI resolves keepassxc://<key> through the Secret Service on the session bus. KeePassXC registers org.freedesktop.secrets when you enable Secret Service integration in the application settings. Give the KeePassXC entry a custom attribute phial with the value <key>. The CLI searches for that attribute and reads the entry secret. Keep the KeePassXC window open and unlocked during lookups.
+
+## Flatpak
+
+The Flatpak manifest at flatpak/com.pojtinger.felicitas.Phial.json builds every runtime dependency from source. Install flatpak-builder, then run make flatpak. Read flatpak/README.md.
+
+The manifest needs the golang and rust-stable SDK extensions. The edk2 module needs network access for its submodules. A full build takes about one hour on twelve cores.
