--- /dev/null
+++ b/flatpak/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# Flatpak
+
+This directory carries the Flatpak manifest for Phial.
+
+## Build
+
+Install the builder:
+
+```sh
+sudo dnf install flatpak-builder
+```
+
+Build the bundle:
+
+```sh
+make flatpak
+```
+
+The bundle lands at `flatpak/phial.flatpak`. Install it with:
+
+```sh
+flatpak install --user flatpak/phial.flatpak
+```
+
+## Modules
+
+The manifest builds every runtime dependency from source. The list follows.
+
+- libtpms and swtpm supply the TPM 2.0 device.
+- socat carries the vsock forwards.
+- passt supplies the user space network.
+- Caddy injects secrets into outbound requests.
+- virtiofsd supplies the host shares.
+- QEMU runs the machine.
+- edk2 supplies the OVMF Secure Boot pair.
+- waypipe renders guest windows on the host.
+- FreeRDP supplies the RDP client.
+- Phial itself is the last module.
+
+## Notes
+
+- The manifest pins every archive with a sha256 sum. Run `make flatpak-lint` to validate the JSON alone.
+- The build needs the golang and rust-stable SDK extensions.
+- The edk2 build needs network access for its submodules.
+- A full build takes about one hour on twelve cores. QEMU and edk2 dominate.
